ct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384626 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384627 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384628 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384629 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384630 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1041 "selection" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384628 13194139536122 true] [17592186384625 1110 #uuid "6975df52-b21a-5a04-958e-e8353d9cf26c" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384626 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536122 true] [17592186384626 1111 #uuid "79ba487f-28c5-5d1b-9e56-d271d9ce9e3d" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384627 1034 "I only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536122 true] [17592186384627 1111 #uuid "add9c991-f8b2-51b5-895e-990ca0db9f35" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384628 1034 "III only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536122 true] [17592186384628 1111 #uuid "5a84ce37-8f0a-5827-939f-9a4330caa90b" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384629 1034 "I and II only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536122 true] [17592186384629 1111 #uuid "181ff9b1-dc77-57c8-8058-5983ffd433d9" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384630 1034 "II only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139536122 true] [17592186384630 1111 #uuid "720e8604-6c59-5755-887f-9bc351c6a1f0" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1017 #edb/ref 17592186384632 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1089 "q-97969" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1100 "If $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A-3I)=4,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0$\n- $A-3I$ is invertible\n- $\\lambda =3$ is an eigenvalue of $A$" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1113 #uuid "c08b449a-000e-584f-a553-bf350d70d374" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384631 1145 "Given a $4\\times 4$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=4=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $4$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=4.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(A-3I) & =4-\\text{rank}(A-3I) \\\\  & =4-4 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A-3I)=0,$ we obtain that $A-3I$ must be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $M=A-3I$ is invertible, then $(A-3I)x=0$ has only zero solution. As a result, $\\lambda =3$ can not be an eigenvalue of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384633 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384634 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384635 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384636 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186384637 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1041 "selection" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186384636 13194139536122 true] [17592186384632 1110 #uuid "0885b831-dde7-5596-ad72-d6e1b784a642" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384633 1034 "II and III only" 13194139536122 true] [17592186384633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 1319413953612